# Line endings, decided once here instead of by whatever core.autocrlf each
# machine happens to have. Without this the same commit shows as a change to
# every line on a machine with a different setting.

# Default: normalise to LF in the repository, let each checkout use its native
# endings. This is what keeps diffs readable on Windows and correct elsewhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never gain a stray carriage return, because a tool reads
# them byte for byte: Inno Setup rejects a CRLF licence file's BOM handling,
# and the workflow's YAML is parsed the same way by every runner.
*.iss   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.isl   text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts run through Windows PowerShell 5.1, which reads a .ps1 as
# ANSI unless the file has a BOM. CRLF is safe here, but pinning it keeps the
# byte content identical between the local run and the CI run.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched by any newline conversion.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.exe   binary
*.pfx   binary